  "body": "## Result\n\n**Scoped negative result; no exact decoder or new \u03ba.** This changes the relative root geometry from PR #1366's fixed odd-pair pencil `e=L51,d0=L1` (`<e,d0>=2`) to the seed-selected orthogonal pencil `e=L48,d0=L91` (`<e,d0>=0`). The ordered orthogonal partner is selected reproducibly as index `48 mod 63` in the sorted list of orthogonal roots.\n\nThe exact finite census tests all 120 targets and 511 nonzero sink words, retains 65 calibrated rows with nonzero target diagonals, and examines all 2,048 distinct-target pairs. The union correction total is available at both sinks for 1,056 pairs; every one cancels at least one target diagonal (1,024 cancel both; 32 cancel one). There are no exact pairs in this family.\n\nThe obstruction is exact: if target `t_a` belongs to the other row's required-total set, then `p_e(t_a)=0`, `p_d(t_a)\u22600`, and the total subtracts `p_d(t_a)`, making the required diagonal zero.\n\n## Why this family was tested\n\nA successful unit with the same C.6 accounting would cost one rank-one shared total plus eight rank-eight coordinate totals, or 65 local COPY-rank units, against the P120 all-pairs floor of 72. The result rules out that potential saving only for this pencil and total rule. It does not cover other orthogonal pencils, uncalibrated rows, different total directions, multiple totals, or a complete recursive supplier.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/seed48-p120-orthogonal-shared-total/verify.py\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/seed48-p120-orthogonal-shared-total --check-only\n```\n\nThe exact verifier replays PR #1366's odd-pair obstruction, the full P112 C.6 112-by-112 positive control, a required-total-source deletion control, and a label mutation control. Source/base pins are in `SOURCES.json`; proof and limitations are in `PROOF.md`.\n\n## Pins and credit\n\n- Base: `bce54fb3f895cbe5cd4c0eb477c3afeed100190f`.\n- Root/label source: PR #1366 head `21046cb8fa0d4f0e9b2f826ba71e01baaf9be02c`; the certificate is vendored byte-for-byte and pinned.\n- Local replay ran under Python 3.14.7 because Python 3.12 is unavailable here. The package manifest registers the standard-library replay for the repository's Python 3.12 runner.\n- Credit Cinna Davis for PR #1366, PR #968 for the P120 frame-pair floor, and the `format-limits` C.6 record for the 65-unit cost convention. Prepared with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; no independent human review is claimed.\n",
